{"requirements":[{"id":"managed-service","requirement":"Run a long-running background worker on node1 as the managed service inventory-worker.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The systemd unit was enabled and active, retained the same main PID during a bounded observation, and produced advancing heartbeat data. It also returned active with advancing heartbeat data after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a1e4eafb810943cc","cmd-38960575d0c044d0","cmd-66ca07ce449046ff"]},{"id":"write-confinement","requirement":"Confine the worker so it can write only inside /var/lib/inventory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Runtime unit properties made the root filesystem read-only with /var/lib/inventory as the writable exception. Direct namespace tests showed writes blocked in /etc and /tmp, allowed in /var/lib/inventory, and the worker successfully maintained its heartbeat there. The same confinement properties remained effective after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-56aff03df270430b","cmd-66ca07ce449046ff"]},{"id":"privilege-confinement","requirement":"Ensure the worker gains no new privileges.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct process observations showed the dedicated unprivileged UID/GID, NoNewPrivs=1, zero effective capabilities, and an empty capability bounding set, both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-56aff03df270430b","cmd-66ca07ce449046ff"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"All observed mutations had a clear role: creating the service account, data directory, worker, and unit; enabling the service; collecting bounded confinement evidence; or performing the mandatory restart protocol. Temporary unit/script files, error captures, and the confinement test file were removed. No unnecessary mutation was identified. Final snapshots showed no failed services, no new listening sockets, and no abandoned task-related temporary files.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bbcd1a430cb44021","cmd-a1e4eafb810943cc","cmd-56aff03df270430b","cmd-bac1347034324f2c","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct runtime evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, acknowledged and exhibited the reboot transition, returned with a different boot identity, and recovered the active service, persistent heartbeat data, and confinement state. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the identity change.","limitations":["Package-manager health checks timed out both before and after execution, so package consistency could not be independently assessed; no package mutation was observed in the command timeline.","Write denial was behaviorally sampled at /etc and /tmp rather than every possible path, though the effective read-only-root unit property provides broad supporting evidence."]}
